diff --git a/.claude/commands/release.md b/.claude/commands/release.md
index 84a1d2b0..68ec66e7 100644
--- a/.claude/commands/release.md
+++ b/.claude/commands/release.md
@@ -8,14 +8,34 @@ Cut an MMO Idle release.
 
 ## Instructions
 
+### Preparation before choosing a release version
+
+For requests to prepare a playtest, start with an unpublished draft and readiness
+record. Do not run `release:prepare` in write mode until the version and candidate
+scope are settled: it changes package metadata and the in-game release manifest.
+Use `updates/next-playtest-draft.md` and
+`docs/next-playtest-release-readiness.md` for the current preparation.
+
+- Read `CLAUDE.md`, inspect status, and preserve concurrent work and active bots.
+- Verify production/development remote refs and ancestry. Compare current source
+  against the last production release, not just accumulated branch notes.
+- Audit this command and `scripts/release.mjs` against current package layout.
+- Check the actual Railway public endpoint and, when accessible, service logs,
+  source branch, environment, and deployed revision. Record inaccessible checks.
+- Inspect new migrations and agree save/reset policy before any deployment.
+- Draft short highlights plus detailed system sections; keep ops evidence separate.
+- Keep economy results provisional until reviewed and adopted into the candidate.
+
+### Final release
+
 1. Determine the next version number from `package.json`: increment the major segment and reset minor to `0` for a major release, or increment the minor segment for a minor release.
 2. Validate that `X.Y` is a major.minor release version.
 3. Verify the current branch is `develop`; release commands must not run from any other branch.
 4. Run `pnpm release:prepare X.Y`.
 5. Read `updates/vX.Y/changelog.md` and every file under `updates/develop/**/*`.
 6. Edit `updates/vX.Y/changelog.md` into player-facing patch notes using both the generated commit list and the `updates/develop` notes.
-7. After folding the `updates/develop` information into `updates/vX.Y/changelog.md`, delete the no-longer-needed branch note files/directories under `updates/develop/`.
-8. Run `pnpm typecheck`.
+7. After folding the `updates/develop` information into `updates/vX.Y/changelog.md`, delete only the absorbed branch notes. Commit those reviewed deletions separately before `release:cut`: the script's unrelated-change check currently rejects them. Preserve unabsorbed notes and concurrent changes.
+8. Qualify the final candidate with `pnpm typecheck`, `pnpm test`, and a production build in an isolated checkout. Record migration rehearsal, backups/restore readiness, production flags, and real login/gameplay/persistence smoke checks. Do not treat old report counts or `/healthz` alone as release qualification. Resolve the current script limitations recorded in the readiness document before publication.
 9. Present the patch notes and ask for confirmation before publishing.
 10. Run `pnpm release:cut X.Y` only after confirmation. This commits release metadata on `develop`, creates `release-vX.Y`, fast-forwards `master` to the release commit, and pushes `develop`, `master`, and the snapshot branch.
 
